mmc: sdhci-sprd: R11P3 (UMS9632) HS200/HS400 tuning and DLL setup, after the vendor driver

The R11P3 host has no SDHCI standard tuning: sdhci_execute_tuning() times out silently (pr_debug only), returns 0
and HS200 runs with an untuned sampling point, so every read fails. Like the Unisoc driver, sweep the DLL
command/read delays in raw DLL steps (compensation off) over 1.5 clock periods with the tuning command, take the
middle of the longest passing window and program it as a phase. Also: DLL phase-internal 2 instead of 3 (the
vendor's CONFIG_MMC_SPRD_SDHCR11P3 value), a bounded wait for the end of a transfer before a reset after a data
error (vendor workaround), and DLL registers in the register dump. Only for "sprd,sdhci-r11p3".

